# ===========================================================================
#  Enterprise Health Dashboard - .gitignore
#
#  The important rule: a GENERATED dashboard contains real data from a real
#  estate - server names, database names, query text, login names, error
#  messages. Only the shipped template is safe to publish.
#
#  Verify before your first commit:
#      git status
#      git check-ignore -v 04-dashboard/estate.html      # should be ignored
#      git check-ignore -v 04-dashboard/dashboard.html   # should NOT be ignored
# ===========================================================================

# --- generated dashboards: REAL DATA, never commit -------------------------
04-dashboard/*.html
estate*.html
*-demo.html

# ...except the template, which ships with sample data and is required by the
# generator. This negation works because no rule excludes 04-dashboard/ itself.
!04-dashboard/dashboard.html

# --- generated documents ---------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate: python deploy/Export-Inventory.py && node deploy/doc3-objects.js
# They also acquire a tenant sensitivity label when created inside OneDrive,
# which makes them unreadable to document tooling.
*.docx
*.pdf

# Screenshots ARE committed - the README embeds them.
!docs/EHD-Docs/screens/*.png

# Superseded preview images from an earlier synthetic estate. Harmless (no real
# data) but they show the old 3-server seed and reference a credential that no
# longer exists. The README uses docs/EHD-Docs/screens/ instead.
04-dashboard/preview-*.png

# Scratch output from reconciling the inventory against a live database
docs/live-objects.txt

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
secrets.json
*.secret
*.key
*.pfx
*.pem
.env
appsettings.*.json
local.settings.json

# --- local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
*.old
*.bak
*.tmp
~$*

# --- tooling ---------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
